  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nThe `swap()` function in the GTELaunchpadV2Pair contract contains a critical vulnerability that allows users to inadvertently lose tokens by sending both token0 and token1 simultaneously. The root cause lies in the flawed input amount calculation logic:\n\n```js\nuint256 amount0In = balance0 > _reserve0 - amount0Out ? balance0 - (_reserve0 - amount0Out) : 0;\nuint256 amount1In = balance1 > _reserve1 - amount1Out ? balance1 - (_reserve1 - amount1Out) : 0;\nif (amount0In == 0 && amount1In == 0) revert(\"UniswapV2: INSUFFICIENT_INPUT_AMOUNT\");\n```\nWhen a user sends both tokens to the contract before calling swap, the calculation can result in one amountIn being zero while the other remains positive. The revert condition only triggers when both amounts are zero, allowing the transaction to proceed with one token being processed normally while the other is effectively lost.\n\n### Impact\n\nSilent Token Loss: Users can lose significant amounts of tokens without receiving any value in return, as the \"lost\" tokens remain in the contract but are not accounted for in reserves or swap calculations.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n- Prevent Dual Token Inputs:\n\n```js\nuint256 amount0In = balance0 > _reserve0 - amount0Out ? balance0 - (_reserve0 - amount0Out) : 0;\nuint256 amount1In = balance1 > _reserve1 - amount1Out ? balance1 - (_reserve1 - amount1Out) : 0;\n\nif (amount0In == 0 && amount1In == 0) revert(\"UniswapV2: INSUFFICIENT_INPUT_AMOUNT\");\n// Add this check to prevent dual token input vulnerability\nif (amount0In > 0 && amount1In > 0) revert(\"UniswapV2: DUAL_TOKEN_INPUT_NOT_ALLOWED\");\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "Add this to the `test/c4-poc` and run `forge test --mt test_Nyxaris_Swap_MultipleTokensIn_Vulnerability -vv `\n```js\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.0;\n\n\nimport {LaunchpadFeePairTest} from \"../../test/launchpad/uniswap/LaunchpadFeePair.t.sol\";\n\nimport \"forge-std/console.sol\";\n\n \ncontract PoCLaunchpad is LaunchpadFeePairTest{\n\n    \n   function test_Nyxaris_Swap_MultipleTokensIn_Vulnerability() public {\n        uint256 amountIn = 10 ether;\n        uint256 extraAmount = 5 ether; // Extra token1 sent\n\n        deal(address(base), address(this), amountIn);\n        deal(address(quote), address(this), extraAmount);\n\n        (uint256 amount0Out, uint256 amount1Out) = getAmountsOut(pair, amountIn, address(base));\n\n        // Record balances before transfers\n        uint256 pairBaseBalanceBefore = base.balanceOf(address(pair));\n        uint256 pairQuoteBalanceBefore = quote.balanceOf(address(pair));\n        uint256 userBaseBalanceBefore = base.balanceOf(address(this));\n        uint256 userQuoteBalanceBefore = quote.balanceOf(address(this));\n\n        // Send both tokens to the pair\n        base.transfer(address(pair), amountIn);\n        quote.transfer(address(pair), extraAmount);\n\n        // Record balances after transfers (before swap)\n        uint256 pairBaseBalanceAfterTransfer = base.balanceOf(address(pair));\n        uint256 pairQuoteBalanceAfterTransfer = quote.balanceOf(address(pair));\n\n        // The swap should succeed despite sending both tokens, demonstrating the vulnerability\n        pair.swap(amount0Out, amount1Out, address(this), hex\"\");\n\n        // Record balances after swap\n        uint256 pairBaseBalanceAfter = base.balanceOf(address(pair));\n        uint256 pairQuoteBalanceAfter = quote.balanceOf(address(pair));\n        uint256 userBaseBalanceAfter = base.balanceOf(address(this));\n        uint256 userQuoteBalanceAfter = quote.balanceOf(address(this));\n\n        // Verify that fee1 is accrued due to the extra token1 being treated as input\n        assertGt(pair.accruedLaunchpadFee1(), 0, \"Fee1 should be accrued from extra token1 input\");\n\n        // The extra token affects the fee calculation, allowing manipulation\n        uint256 normalFee1 = _calculateExpectedLaunchpadFee(amountIn, address(base)); // For amountIn of base\n        assertGt(pair.accruedLaunchpadFee1(), normalFee1 / 10, \"Fee1 is significantly higher due to extra input\");\n\n        \n    }\n\n    \n}\n\n```",
